---
import IntakeFormCta from "./IntakeFormCta.astro";
---

<section
  class="rounded-2xl border border-brand-border bg-brand-surface p-5 shadow-sm sm:p-6"
  aria-labelledby="schema-upload-help"
>
  <h2 id="schema-upload-help" class="text-lg font-semibold text-brand-primary">
    How to export your schema
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-brand-secondary">
    No live database connection. Export table and column definitions, then upload one
    <strong class="font-medium text-brand-primary">.zip</strong> file (both CSVs inside) on the
    intake form.
  </p>

  <details class="mt-4 text-sm text-brand-secondary">
    <summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-brand-primary">
      Postgres — easiest options
    </summary>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
      <li>
        <strong class="text-brand-primary">pgAdmin / DBeaver:</strong> run each query below,
        then use <em>Export / Save results as CSV</em> to your Downloads folder.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-brand-primary">psql:</strong> run the queries, copy results, or use
        <code class="rounded bg-brand-bg px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">\copy (...)</code> to save into your
        current folder (no <code class="rounded bg-brand-bg px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">/tmp</code>).
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-brand-muted">
      Zip <code class="rounded bg-brand-bg px-1">semlay_schema_columns.csv</code> and
      <code class="rounded bg-brand-bg px-1">semlay_schema_keys.csv</code> before uploading.
    </p>
  </details>

  <details class="mt-3 text-sm text-brand-secondary">
    <summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-brand-primary">SQL to run (Postgres)</summary>
    <pre
      class="mt-3 max-h-64 overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-brand-border bg-brand-bg p-3 text-xs leading-relaxed text-brand-primary"><code>{`-- 1) Tables and columns → save as semlay_schema_columns.csv
SELECT table_schema, table_name, column_name, data_type, is_nullable
FROM information_schema.columns
WHERE table_schema NOT IN ('pg_catalog', 'information_schema')
ORDER BY table_schema, table_name, ordinal_position;

-- 2) Keys and constraints → save as semlay_schema_keys.csv
SELECT tc.table_schema, tc.table_name, tc.constraint_type, kcu.column_name,
       ccu.table_schema AS foreign_table_schema,
       ccu.table_name AS foreign_table_name,
       ccu.column_name AS foreign_column_name
FROM information_schema.table_constraints tc
LEFT JOIN information_schema.key_column_usage kcu
  ON tc.constraint_name = kcu.constraint_name
 AND tc.table_schema = kcu.table_schema
LEFT JOIN information_schema.constraint_column_usage ccu
  ON tc.constraint_name = ccu.constraint_name
WHERE tc.table_schema NOT IN ('pg_catalog', 'information_schema');`}</code></pre>
  </details>

  <div class="mt-6 sm:hidden">
    <IntakeFormCta class="w-full" label="Continue to form" />
  </div>
</section>
